the cyclical nature of the homebuilding industry, which is particularly susceptible to economic changes, either nationally or in the regional and local markets in which we operate, including continued elevated and any future increases in interest rates and the resulting impact on the accessibility and cost of mortgage loans to homebuyers; persistent inflation; decreased employment levels and job insecurity concerns due in part to the rapid adoption of artificial intelligence; cautious consumer sentiment; affordability concerns; and increased recessionary conditions;

